---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Summer School"
  description="The Oxford LLMs Summer School: a five-day intensive on LLMs for social science at Nuffield College, Oxford. Four editions since 2023; the 2026 school ran 13–17 July."
>

  <!-- ── Hero: the school, told in photographs ──────────────── -->
  <header class="hero-event">
    <div class="hero-rule-top"></div>
    <div class="hero-event-inner">

      <div class="event-content">
        <div class="ed-kicker">Nuffield College, Oxford</div>
        <h1 class="h-title">
          A five-day intensive for early-career social scientists
          working with language models.
        </h1>
        <p class="lede-v3" style="margin-bottom:22px;">
          Mornings: technical lectures from ML practitioners and invited researchers.
          Afternoons: hands-on labs and a week-long collaborative research project.
          Tuition is free for all admitted participants.
        </p>

        <p class="copy" style="margin:0 0 28px; color:var(--text-sec); max-width:56ch;">
          The fourth edition ran 13&ndash;17 July 2026. Dates and applications for 2027
          will be announced here.
        </p>

        <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/summer-school/2026/">
            2026 highlights <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href="#past">
            Past cohorts <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="event-gallery">
        <img class="eg-lead" src="/img/posts/report_2026/lecture_hall_2026.jpg"
             alt="A lecture in progress in the Nuffield College lecture room, seen from the back" />
        <img src="/img/posts/report_2026/research_table_2026.jpg"
             alt="A team working together at a long table during an afternoon research session" />
        <img src="/img/posts/report_2026/social_2026.jpg"
             alt="Participants working and talking informally in a college common room" />
        <figcaption>Oxford LLMs 2026, Nuffield College</figcaption>
      </figure>

    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ── Stats ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section style="padding: clamp(20px,2.5vw,36px) 0 clamp(40px,5vw,64px);">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="stats-v3 reveal">
        <div class="stat-v3">
          <span class="stat-n">4th</span>
          <span class="stat-l">Year running</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-v3">
          <span class="stat-n">30</span>
          <span class="stat-l">Places</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-v3">
          <span class="stat-n">5</span>
          <span class="stat-l">Days</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-v3">
          <span class="stat-n">£0</span>
          <span class="stat-l">Tuition fee</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── § 01 Past cohorts ──────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section-v3 section-v3--marker" id="past">
    <span class="section-number">§ 01 · Past cohorts</span>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head-v3 reveal">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow-v3" style="margin-bottom:14px">Four years in</div>
          <h2 class="h-section">A participant-to-co-author pipeline.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lede-v3">
          The school is designed around a participant-to-co-author pipeline.
          Collaborative projects begun during the week continue beyond it: in 2025, a team of
          participants and speakers submitted a joint paper for peer review.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cohort-timeline reveal">

        <a class="cohort-entry" href="/summer-school/2026/">
          <div class="ce-content">
            <span class="ce-year">2026</span>
            <span class="ce-edition">Fourth edition · July 2026</span>
            <h3 class="ce-title">Six teams. A week-long common-task challenge.</h3>
            <p class="ce-desc">
              A technical programme taught by practitioners from Meta, Nebius, and Liquid.AI,
              wrapped around the AI Respondents Challenge: six teams predicting individual survey
              responses, scored on progressively harder held-out data through the week.
            </p>
            <span class="btn-link-v3">Read the 2026 highlights <span class="arrow">→</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ce-photo">
            <img src="/img/posts/report_2026/group_photo_2026.jpg"
                 alt="Oxford LLMs 2026 cohort at Nuffield College" />
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="cohort-entry" href="/summer-school/2025/">
          <div class="ce-content">
            <span class="ce-year">2025</span>
            <span class="ce-edition">Third edition · September 2025</span>
            <h3 class="ce-title">30 researchers. A prediction competition. One paper submitted.</h3>
            <p class="ce-desc">
              Lectures on LLM fundamentals, evaluation, fine-tuning, AI agents, and AI safety.
              A Kaggle-style prediction competition ran alongside the research project.
              A team of participants and speakers continued the work after September and submitted
              it for peer review.
            </p>
            <span class="btn-link-v3">Read the 2025 highlights <span class="arrow">→</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ce-photo">
            <img src="/img/posts/report_2025/group_photo_2025.jpg"
                 alt="Oxford LLMs 2025 cohort at Nuffield College" />
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="cohort-entry" href="/summer-school/2024/">
          <div class="ce-content">
            <span class="ce-year">2024</span>
            <span class="ce-edition">Second edition · September 2024</span>
            <h3 class="ce-title">30 participants from ~200 applications.</h3>
            <p class="ce-desc">
              Applied tutorials on RAG, observability, and agent-based systems.
              A cross-discipline line-up of NLP engineers, social scientists, and
              practitioners from Qdrant, Ori Cloud, Arize, and Google.
            </p>
            <span class="btn-link-v3">Read the 2024 highlights <span class="arrow">→</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ce-photo">
            <img src="/img/posts/report_2024/group_llms_2024.jpg"
                 alt="Oxford LLMs 2024 cohort at Nuffield College" />
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="cohort-entry" href="/summer-school/2023/">
          <div class="ce-content">
            <span class="ce-year">2023</span>
            <span class="ce-edition">Inaugural edition · September 2023</span>
            <h3 class="ce-title">The first Oxford LLMs workshop.</h3>
            <p class="ce-desc">
              Convened by Elena Voita and Ilya Boytsov for a cohort of ~30 early-career
              researchers exploring transformers, text-as-data methods, and the emerging
              landscape of large language models.
            </p>
            <span class="btn-link-v3">Read the 2023 highlights <span class="arrow">→</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="ce-photo">
            <img src="/img/posts/report_2023/group_llms_2023.jpg"
                 alt="Oxford LLMs 2023 inaugural cohort at Nuffield College" />
          </div>
        </a>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── § 02 Materials ────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section-v3 section-v3--marker section-tinted-v3" id="materials"
           style="padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 7vw, 88px);">
    <span class="section-number">§ 02 · Materials</span>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head-v3 reveal">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow-v3" style="margin-bottom:14px">Open access</div>
          <h2 class="h-section">Slides and notebooks from past editions.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lede-v3">
          All lecture slides and coding materials are published openly after each edition.
          Datasets and model checkpoints from collaborative research projects are on Hugging Face.
          Materials go up as speakers clear them, and we are editing the lecture and research talk
          recordings for open release. Watch this space.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 20px;"
           class="reveal-stagger">

        <article class="fb">
          <span class="rule-soft"></span>
          <div class="eyebrow-v3" style="margin-bottom:10px">2026 · Fourth edition</div>
          <h3 class="h-sub" style="margin-bottom:14px">Lecture slides &amp; challenge</h3>
          <p class="copy" style="margin:0 0 14px; font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">
            Lectures on agents and evaluation, continual learning, and LLM data and RL environments,
            plus the AI Respondents Challenge dataset and starter kit. More sessions are being
            cleared for release.
          </p>
          <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
            <a class="btn-link-v3" href="https://github.com/Oxford-LLMs-Research/oxford-llms-workshop"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px;">
              <img src="/img/icons/github-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:15px; height:15px; opacity:0.75; flex-shrink:0;">
              GitHub repository <span class="arrow">→</span>
            </a>
            <a class="btn-link-v3" href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/oxford-llms/ai-respondents-challenge"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px;">
              <img src="/img/icons/hf-logo.svg" alt="" style="width:15px; height:15px; flex-shrink:0;">
              Challenge dataset <span class="arrow">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="fb">
          <span class="rule-soft"></span>
          <div class="eyebrow-v3" style="margin-bottom:10px">2025 · Third edition</div>
          <h3 class="h-sub" style="margin-bottom:14px">Coding seminars</h3>
          <p class="copy" style="margin:0 0 14px; font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">
            Hands-on notebooks on LLM fundamentals and on post-training: supervised fine-tuning,
            DPO, and GRPO. Remaining lecture slides are being collected from speakers.
          </p>
          <a class="btn-link-v3" href="https://github.com/Oxford-LLMs-Research/oxford-llms-workshop"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px;">
            <img src="/img/icons/github-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:15px; height:15px; opacity:0.75; flex-shrink:0;">
            GitHub repository <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="fb">
          <span class="rule-soft"></span>
          <div class="eyebrow-v3" style="margin-bottom:10px">2024 · Second edition</div>
          <h3 class="h-sub" style="margin-bottom:14px">Slides, notebooks &amp; datasets</h3>
          <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
            <a class="btn-link-v3" href="https://github.com/Oxford-LLMs-Research/oxford-llms-workshop"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px;">
              <img src="/img/icons/github-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:15px; height:15px; opacity:0.75; flex-shrink:0;">
              GitHub repository <span class="arrow">→</span>
            </a>
            <a class="btn-link-v3" href="https://huggingface.co/oxford-llms"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px;">
              <img src="/img/icons/hf-logo.svg" alt="" style="width:15px; height:15px; flex-shrink:0;">
              Hugging Face <span class="arrow">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="fb">
          <span class="rule-soft"></span>
          <div class="eyebrow-v3" style="margin-bottom:10px">2023 · Inaugural</div>
          <h3 class="h-sub" style="margin-bottom:14px">Slides &amp; notebooks</h3>
          <a class="btn-link-v3" href="https://github.com/Oxford-LLMs-Research/oxford-llms-workshop"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px;">
            <img src="/img/icons/github-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:15px; height:15px; opacity:0.75; flex-shrink:0;">
            GitHub repository <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
